# Calibrate print and scan round trips

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical report primitives are not measurements. Finite acceptance below
permits theory-only evidence without claiming a measured performance result.

Measure physical scale, clipping, margins, grid registration, color shifts,
photo placement, line weight, and scanner distortion on representative devices.

Current executable evidence now names all eight physical round-trip measurement
families explicitly and keeps each caller-owned observation tied to its source,
unit, value, and rendered/exported output identity. The four ADR verification
families remain physical scale, clipping, grid registration, and photo
placement; P5 additionally retains margins, color shift, line weight, and
scanner distortion.

Structural admission now requires at least one observation for every family and
returns constructor-sealed evidence borrowing the exact complete set. Repeated
measurements remain valid. An exhaustive 256-mask oracle requires the direct and
sealed paths to report the first missing family in canonical requirement order
without interpreting any observation as calibration success.

Representative-device selection, concrete units, tolerances, statistical
analysis, correction transforms, calibration fitting, and pass/fail policy
remain open.

## Finite one-sheet print/scan calibration and quality rubric

**Inputs:** one fully rendered and authorized A4 PDF artifact and manifest,
a declared printer/driver/paper configuration, a scanner/camera with stable
settings, and one raw captured physical output. **Outputs:** eight
source-linked measurement families plus a measured correction/refusal
report, or `TheoryOnly` when no physical hardware evidence is available.
No software-only vector plan may be called a successful printer calibration.

**A4 target chart:** print one `210 x 297 mm` page at actual size with four
registration crosses 15 mm from each corner, a horizontal 100 mm reference
ruler, a 2 x 2 line grid, 0.2/0.4 mm stroke gauges, RGB/gray swatches, one
50 x 40 mm placed photo region, and labeled 20 mm margins. Record actual
printer scaling, tray/page orientation, ink/paper and scan resolution before
measuring. Device-specific settings must stay attached to every observation.

**Eight measurement dimensions:**

| Family | One recorded observation | Proposed review bound |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Physical scale | Measured 100 mm ruler | 99..101 mm |
| Clipping | Missing boundary/chart marks | Zero omitted marks |
| Margins | Minimum marked inset | Within 1 mm of target |
| Grid registration | Largest corner residual | At most 1 mm |
| Color shift | Swatch versus reference | Declared calibrated comparison |
| Photo placement | Center displacement | At most 1 mm |
| Line weight | Measured 0.4 mm gauge | Within 0.1 mm |
| Scanner distortion | Residual after alignment | At most 1 mm |

**Capture/report rule:** retain eight observed source/capture IDs, units,
method and uncorrected measurements, then compare against declared
reference geometry. Estimate one explicit correction transform only from
held-out reference marks, not from handwriting shapes being graded. A
missing color calibration target yields `UnmeasuredColor`, not a fabricated
color tolerance. Corrections may be proposed to a new output profile but
must not mutate the source notebook or original scanner capture.

**Worked example:** a hypothetical print of the 100 mm ruler measures 100.6
mm; the largest registration error is 0.7 mm and line weight measures 0.45
mm. Those three *illustrative* observations fall inside their provisional
bounds; the other five remain unmeasured and therefore the report is
`Incomplete`, not `Calibrated`. With no printer/scanner, all eight families
are specified theoretically and the acceptance is `TheoryOnly`.

**Refusal example:** a report has no clipping observation, actual-size print
was silently fit to paper, scans are distorted beyond the declared model,
or source output revision differs from the measurement manifest. Retain
reported failures and request a new capture; never fix layout by silently
changing page scale or claiming a device passed without measured evidence.

**Assumptions and limits:** existing data types require all eight physical
measurement families with owner/source/units, but cannot measure or grade a
printer. Device selection, scanner alignment, color science, tolerance
calibration and profile correction are unimplemented. Theoretical protocol
acceptance does not certify any physical print or scanner.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for eight-axis evidence completeness; theoretical
  for hardware capture and correction, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one A4 target sheet, eight finite measurements, proposed
  bounds, example incomplete report and hardware-absent `TheoryOnly` state.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** print/scan execution,
  device calibration, measured tolerances or verified output fidelity.
